>
> Any idea ?

If it's like my PWS500au, it's got a "Silicon Image, Inc. PCI0646 (rev 01)"=
=20
IDE controller in it that is as buggy as I'll get out.  Maybe try the=20
ide_generic module.  It works for me on 2.6.14.

I stopped using the cmd64x module quite a while ago.  It enabled DMAing, wh=
ich=20
resulted in random corruption on my backup IDE harddisk.  Maybe enabling it=
=20
has some sort of interupt problem as well.

