Before you try to get another card, know that I have run Xorg on an=20
Alpha XL366 (XLT) with a Matrox Millennium II and a Matrox Mystique.=20
Both ran well enough considering their age and the relative speed of the=20
machine. I used the MGA driver.

I got that message once too, and all I had to do was to specify the PCI=20
BusID for the card. You can use lspci to get your card's BusID and then=20
put it in your xorg.conf (or XF86Config-4.conf or something) in the=20
device section. Search Google or read the conf file's man page for more=20
details, I can't remember exactly.

The only pesky problem I got with those cards was graphical corruption=20
everywhere on the screen when I would run Gnome. Under KDE everything=20
was fine though. I no longer run anything graphical on that machine=20
though, it was quite slow in X.

Good luck,

J-S

