On Wed, Feb 22, 2006 at 06:40:06PM +0100, Jarno Saarinen wrote:
> 
> I have just installed Debian 3.1 (sarge) on my Digital Personal Workstation 
> 600au but I still have a (BIG) problem: I cannot make the network work.
> 
> .....
>
> I suspect (but I do not know if I am correct) that the problem could
> be in the (integrated) ethernet card. It has both a BNC and a RJ45
> plug and I use the second one to connect to the LAN.

Since it has a BNC connector, it probably is the slow NIC, ie tulip
21040/21041 chipset. Those work better, IMHO, with the "de4x5" driver,
rather than the "dc2104x" driver. Try switching to "de4x5" and see if
it works any better.

Good luck.

