On Fri, 24 Feb 2006 11:55:52 +0100 (MET)
Jarno Saarinen <jarno.saarinen@infinito.it> wrote:

> Hi,
> 
> I have a new problem in setting up Debian Sarge on a Digital Personal 
> Workstation 600au. In particular, I cannot make the graphical
> environment start. I think that it depends on the fact that linux
> cannot detect (or, correctly recognize) the graphical card.

Hi!

You will probably need to set the BusID in your XF86Config.
Find a line like this:
    BusID      "PCI:0:10:0"
and put in, what lspci gives you as ID for your graphics card.

HTH,

Marc



