> What you have in your box is an Integraph Powerstorm 4D50T, an option
> that DEC OEM'ed, a high-end card that includes a Cirrus Logic (simple)
> VGA to perform text mode operation.
>
> There IS NO DRIVER for the Integraph accelerator, and I believe there
> may be no (current) driver for the Cirrus. And even if there IS, it
> most likely only has 512K (yes, K!) of video memory attached to it.
>
> My recommendation: find a nice Permedia-2 or Matrox Millennium card
> and pull the 4D50T and sell it on Ebay... ;-}
>
> Unless, of course, you're willing to run only VMS or Tru64 on there,
> and then that card would be OK...
>
> Good luck.
